  "body": "Add shared Rust `G93` inverse-time feed calculation and explicit section mode metadata so posts handle 3-axis, 3+2 indexed, and simultaneous 5-axis sections separately.\n\n### Context\n- `crates/post/src/post/rotary_cap.rs` computes only `G94` feed caps today.\n- Under `G93` in Mach4 and RS-274/NGC, `F = 1 / dt_min` (`min^-1`) applies per block, and every feed block requires an `F` word.\n- Today the `.cnc` stream does not state explicitly whether a tilted section is 3+2 indexed (`Tilt` in `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs`) or simultaneous 5-axis (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/mod.rs`).\n\n### Requirements\n- Emit explicit section mode parameters distinguishing 3-axis, 3+2 indexed, and simultaneous 5-axis without breaking existing `.cl` or golden inputs.\n- Compute per-block `dt_cut = ||tip_1 - tip_0|| / v_prog` in part space, plus `dt_lim` from stated linear and rotary `max_normal_speed` ceilings in `min^-1`.\n- Take `dt_min = max(dt_cut, dt_lim)`, handle rotary-only reorientations without division by zero, skip zero-motion duplicate moves, and clamp `F = 1 / dt_min` to safe bounds.\n- Keep `G93` `F` independent of `G20` (inch) vs `G21` (mm).\n\nDone means: Simultaneous post segments receive finite `G93` `F` values honoring linear and rotary speed limits in both mm and inch, zero-length moves never fail or divide by zero, 3+2 sections stay distinct from simultaneous sections, and 3-axis streams stay unchanged.\n\nPart of #1958\n",
